Package: epiIngest
Type: Package
Title: Multi-Source Ingestion and Rule-Based Quality Control for Surveillance Counts
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("EpiStack", "Authors", email = "epistack@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: EpiStack Authors [aut, cre]
Maintainer: EpiStack Authors <epistack@example.com>
Description: Ingestion layer (L1) of the EpiStack ecosystem. Reads surveillance
    counts from delimited text files and, optionally, from Excel workbooks,
    database queries, HTTP endpoints and raster covariates, then applies a
    declarative quality-control rule set with per-row audit trails. Rules are
    data, not code, so a project can version its own rule file. Output is the
    versioned long-table contract consumed by every downstream layer.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0)
Imports: utils, stats, tools
Suggests: epiCore, readxl, openxlsx, DBI, terra, openssl, digest
NeedsCompilation: no
URL: https://github.com/Rythonme/EpiStack
BugReports: https://github.com/Rythonme/EpiStack/issues
